      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.68,
      "end": 2.3,
      "text": "Hello, how are things going?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.05,
      "end": 17.54,
      "text": "Many countries accept home photos if you meet the rules. Check your passport office's list, but the usual ones are plain light background, even lighting and a neutral face."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 22.11,
      "end": 27.23,
      "text": "Usually, yes. Mouth closed, eyes open, no glasses, looking straight at the camera."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 31.6,
      "end": 35.31,
      "text": "Let me double-check. I'd still stand by it, but tell me what you heard."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 40.21,
      "end": 47.04,
      "text": "Beige can fail. Stand in front of a white door or tape a white sheet up, and face a window so there are no shadows behind you."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 50.41,
      "end": 56.15,
      "text": "Better than a selfie, actually. Have him stand about a metre and a half away at your eye level, so your face isn't distorted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 61.72,
      "end": 66.17,
      "text": "Even with no smile, a relaxed face helps. Take a few and pick the calmest one."
    }
